    faq_label:"FAQ", faq_title:`<span class="title-bold">Everything you need to know about </span><strong>micropigmentation</strong>`,
    faq_1_q:"What is scalp micropigmentation (SMP)?", faq_1_a:"Scalp micropigmentation is a non-surgical technique that deposits pigment into the upper layer of the scalp dermis to recreate the appearance of hair follicles. The result is a natural shaved look or visible density in thinning areas.",
    faq_2_q:"How many sessions are needed?", faq_2_a:"In general, 2 to 3 sessions are required, spaced 7 to 14 days apart. In some cases, a 4th session may be needed. The exact number depends on the area treated, skin type and desired result. All necessary sessions are included in the initial price.",
    faq_3_q:"Is it painful?", faq_3_a:"The procedure is generally well tolerated. The sensation is similar to a light tingling that usually fades as the session progresses.",
    faq_4_q:"How long do the results last?", faq_4_a:"Results are long-lasting. To maintain an optimal result, a small touch-up session every 1 to 3 years is recommended.",
    faq_5_q:"Is there any recovery time?", faq_5_a:"Recovery time is minimal. You can resume normal activities the same day. It is recommended to avoid sun exposure and intense activity for a few days after each session.",
    faq_6_q:"Is micropigmentation suitable for all skin types?", faq_6_a:"Yes, scalp micropigmentation is suitable for all skin types. Pigments and techniques are adjusted according to skin tone and hair colour to ensure a natural and harmonious result.",
    faq_7_q:"Are hair transplants and tricopigmentation compatible?", faq_7_a:"Yes, they are complementary. Tricopigmentation can improve the result of a hair transplant and is also suitable for people who are not good candidates for hair transplantation.",
    faq_8_q:"What about touch-ups?", faq_8_a:"A preferential touch-up rate is offered between 1 and 3 years after the initial procedure, provided that the procedure was performed in our studio.",
    faq_9_q:"How does payment work?", faq_9_a:"Payment can be made upfront or in several instalments throughout your procedure. A deposit is required to confirm your appointment.",

